WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.920
The aftershock shuddered through the&nbsp;
Foundation, emergency alarms wailed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.880
as injured staff and security helped each&nbsp;
other out from underneath rubble that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:14.040
fallen on them as the building was shaken by the&nbsp;
quake. It had only lasted a few short seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:20.460
but still managed to leave a trail of destruction&nbsp;
in its wake. While the wounded were bandaged up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.860
anyone and everyone who was still able to&nbsp;
started frantically checking the containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.320
of every anomaly on the site. The Foundation could&nbsp;
worry about the origin of the quake later. First&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:37.380
and foremost, they needed to assess the damage.
Luckily, multiple rapid sweeps of the facility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.400
revealed that there weren’t all that many&nbsp;
high-threat level anomalies whose containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.200
had been breached. A few of the safer ones&nbsp;
were found cowering under tables, or buried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.300
under fallen rubble in their quarters. But, for&nbsp;
the most part, every anomaly was accounted for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.820
and none had been provided with an opportunity&nbsp;
to escape and cause further havoc. At least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.800
that’s how things seemed at first.
It was only when the chaos started to die down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.220
and repair efforts went underway that personnel&nbsp;
noticed an odd change. Something was missing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.020
but nobody could quite put their finger&nbsp;
on exactly what. As a matter of fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:19.020
most could pinpoint exactly when they noticed this&nbsp;
odd feeling: it had only begun after the emergency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:25.080
alarms had been shut off. There was a sound that&nbsp;
everyone working at the Foundation had gotten so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:30.900
used to that they’d practically stopped hearing&nbsp;
it, or at least, they’d stopped noticing it.&nbsp;

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:36.840
It was only now that the noise was gone, its&nbsp;
absence no longer drowned out by blaring alarms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.900
that staff realized. It had always been there;&nbsp;
everyone had just learned to subconsciously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.760
tune it out:
Crying.&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:51.600
The low, soft whimpering that could often be heard&nbsp;
emanating from SCP-096’s containment chamber. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:57.480
had stopped. The cell within had fallen silent.&nbsp;
And, once someone at the Foundation made the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:06.000
connection and investigated, they happened upon a&nbsp;
startling discovery. SCP-096 had vanished. Panic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.040
immediately engulfed the facility yet again.&nbsp;
The Shy Guy could be anywhere, and a search&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.080
effort to find it would only end in deaths.
After all, in order to find something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:22.140
you have to look at it, and that was a&nbsp;
fatal thing to do when SCP-096 was involved.&nbsp;

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.600
Closer examination showed no trace of the missing&nbsp;
creature. There had been no reported incidents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.460
of incursions with it from anywhere in the&nbsp;
world. Every known photograph, video recording,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:38.640
or other visual depiction of SCP-096 was either&nbsp;
securely stashed away or destroyed completely by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.040
the Foundation. There was no way it could have&nbsp;
possibly escaped, and it was seemingly nowhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:49.440
at all. But still, the question remained:&nbsp;
where in the world had the Shy Guy gone to?&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:56.280
If it was still even in this world.
From SCP-096’s perspective, one moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:02.280
all had been normal. The next, it was lost&nbsp;
somewhere strange, unfamiliar, and above all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:08.400
unsettling, even to the Shy Guy. Before the sudden&nbsp;
quake had hit, it had spent the day the same way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.980
it usually occupied its time; alternating between&nbsp;
aimlessly pacing the far wall of its containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:18.900
chamber, and sitting in a fetal position in&nbsp;
the corner, sobbing all the while. But then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.880
the room had started shaking, and in the&nbsp;
blink of a deeply sunken eye, the Shy Guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:29.820
found itself… well, it had no idea where.
Around it was a large, carpeted room, open&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:36.240
and sparse, with little occupying all the space.&nbsp;
The wallpaper was a nauseating, sickly shade of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.400
yellow, made all the more garish by the rows of&nbsp;
fluorescent lighting from the ceiling above. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.380
entire place seemed to resemble an office space,&nbsp;
although seemingly one that was in a total state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:52.500
of disuse. There was no furniture, not even one&nbsp;
solitary, inanimate object to make the place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:59.400
seem at least the tiniest bit closer to normal.
Little was SCP-096 aware, it had somehow been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:06.180
transported to a strange and terrible place:&nbsp;
the Backrooms. Unless someone remains wary and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.700
ever-vigilant, they can unknowingly slip their&nbsp;
way out of reality. It can happen anywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:17.040
all that a person needs to do is be in the&nbsp;
wrong place at the wrong time, and they will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:24.060
noclip into the Backrooms. All around SCP-096 was&nbsp;
the stench of old, wet carpet, and a labyrinth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:29.700
of uninhabited rooms with the same drab yellow&nbsp;
walls, the endless buzz of the fluorescent lights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.640
stretching out for who knows how many square&nbsp;
miles of empty rooms. In short, the Shy Guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:41.340
was trapped in a purgatory-like nightmare.
However, there was at least one small mercy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:47.580
for SCP-096 as it wandered around its new&nbsp;
surroundings. There was nobody else around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:54.900
no other signs of life. No SCP Foundation,&nbsp;
no ordinary human beings, no one who could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:02.100
see it. Here, in the solitary confinement of&nbsp;
the Backrooms, SCP-096 could not be perceived.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.420
And yet, this brought the self-conscious&nbsp;
creature very little in the way of comfort.&nbsp;

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:12.420
Despite being completely alone, there was an&nbsp;
awful, lingering feeling that hung in the air like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:19.140
the smell of the old carpet underfoot. SCP-096&nbsp;
still felt like it was being watched. And yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.940
if someone – or something – really was&nbsp;
watching, it wasn’t triggering the Shy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.020
Guy’s usual rage state. As it lurked&nbsp;
through the various rooms and corridors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:33.420
the creature kept expecting to find someone, to&nbsp;
look them in the eye directly and get that same,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:39.540
inescapable urge to race towards its observer&nbsp;
and kill them. But it never came, because there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:45.780
was nobody else around. At least, for a while.
Adam Jenkins had been just out riding his bike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.640
when it happened. Pushing one pedal around,&nbsp;
then the other, he gradually climbed higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.240
up the slope of a hill. His house was&nbsp;
down at the bottom on the other side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:59.940
and Adam knew, once he reached the peak, he could&nbsp;
slip nice and easily down the rest of the way. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:04.800
long as he was careful not to let the extra&nbsp;
momentum carry his bike too far and too fast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:10.380
he just had to keep in control and gently&nbsp;
compress the brake if he needed to. He made this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:16.260
same journey every day, nothing could go wrong…
Sure enough, Adam reached the top of the hill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:21.540
and allowed the bike to slowly tip ever&nbsp;
so slightly over the other side. Gravity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:26.520
started to do the rest, the wheels starting to&nbsp;
spin rapidly, the pedals pistoning his legs as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:31.860
he plummeted downwards. It was one of the few&nbsp;
childlike joys left in Adam’s life, those few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.480
brief seconds of the day where he got to speed&nbsp;
down the hill back home with reckless abandon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:41.700
He was blissfully unaware that he wouldn’t have&nbsp;
enough time to miss how much he enjoyed it.&nbsp;

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:46.860
Without warning, a car came speeding out from&nbsp;
around a corner on the way down the hill. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:51.960
was dark, and the driver had carelessly decided to&nbsp;
leave their headlights off. So, when Adam saw the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.420
vehicle, he only had a split second to react. He&nbsp;
was still going too fast, so he applied the brakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:02.340
now, his front wheel would stop too suddenly&nbsp;
and send him flying forward over the handlebars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:07.260
Instead, seconds before colliding with the car’s&nbsp;
hood, Adam wrenched his bike’s handlebars and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:12.300
swerved around the car. But the added speed of&nbsp;
going downhill caused the entire bike to topple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:17.460
as it turned so violently, launching Adam off&nbsp;
and sending him hurtling towards a nearby wall.&nbsp;

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:21.840
Adam could tell, in the split second after&nbsp;
coming off his bike, that he was about to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.340
collide with the wall. His brain and body&nbsp;
anticipated the impact, bracing him for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:32.040
the painful crash. But it never came. Instead&nbsp;
of hitting the wall, Adam passed through it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:37.980
That may well have spared him a devastating&nbsp;
injury, but now a whole new problem now faced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.840
him. Just like no clipping through a virtual&nbsp;
environment in a video game, Adam had passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:49.260
directly out of reality… right into the Backrooms.
The first few hours were the worst, shouting as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:54.840
loud as he could for someone, anyone to come and&nbsp;
find him. Each yell rapidly growing more and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.840 --> 00:08:00.780
frantic as Adam rushed around his haunting new&nbsp;
surroundings. The whole place was unsettling just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:06.540
to be in, it gave off a hostile, unwelcoming&nbsp;
energy that was impossible to ignore. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:12.540
only after an hour of trying to find a way out&nbsp;
that Adam realized: he was well and truly lost.&nbsp;

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:18.120
He’d strayed too far away from his original point&nbsp;
of entry, and just as he had the idea of trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:23.220
to make his way back to the world from the same&nbsp;
place he came in, it was already too late. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:28.620
Backrooms - at least on this first level - all&nbsp;
looked the same, no two rooms were distinct enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:33.840
for him to figure out if this was somewhere&nbsp;
he’d been before, or an entirely new area.&nbsp;

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:39.420
It didn’t take long for an overwhelming sense of&nbsp;
hopelessness to set in. Adam had quickly given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:45.060
up calling for help: there was no sign of anyone&nbsp;
around that would be able to help him. Until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.460
shuffling of footsteps came from nearby. It was&nbsp;
such a noticeable break in the dull, unsettling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:55.860
quiet of the Backrooms that it made Adam’s ear’s&nbsp;
prick up. The yellow-hued maze had been so void of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:01.920
life since he arrived, so unnaturally empty, that&nbsp;
he wasn’t entirely sure he hadn’t made the sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:08.340
himself, by his jacket brushing up against a wall.
But no, there was definitely something here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:14.160
with him, he could hear it wandering about&nbsp;
nearby. And it had certainly heard him too.&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.980
Calling out again, with more caution in his&nbsp;
tone, Adam Jenkins turned the next corner, met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:25.920
with yet another dingy yellow corridor. Although,&nbsp;
unlike the others, this one had a key difference:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:32.880
SCP-096 stood right in the middle of it. The split&nbsp;
second that Adam’s eyes fell over the Shy Guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:38.280
it was already too late. He barely had time to&nbsp;
process the sight of the creature; it’s tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:44.460
humanoid shape, wiry thin and pale-skinned,&nbsp;
jaw hanging unnaturally wide. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:50.640
SCP-096 dashed towards Adam so quickly, that&nbsp;
he couldn’t even finish his startled scream…&nbsp;

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.740
Meanwhile, back at the SCP Foundation, efforts&nbsp;
were still underway to retrieve the Shy Guy.&nbsp;

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:59.700
Researchers were baffled that there was&nbsp;
not a single trace anywhere on the globe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:05.400
of SCP-096’s presence. They had quickly rolled out&nbsp;
their usual method for recalling the creature to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.960
containment. Requisitioning one of D Class&nbsp;
personnel, this individual was instructed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:16.200
to stand in SCP-096’s cell and then given a&nbsp;
photograph of the monster to look at. Knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:21.840
that the Shy Guy would track down anyone that&nbsp;
saw its face – even as a single, tiny pixel in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:27.120
a picture – the Foundation expected the creature&nbsp;
to simply reappear in its containment chamber to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:32.280
kill the D Class that they had used as bait.
But nothing happened. The D Class was able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:38.100
to look at the photo of SCP-096 and survive. It&nbsp;
was almost as if the creature’s link to reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.960
was weakened; wherever it was, it might&nbsp;
still be aware someone had looked at it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:48.540
but the Shy Guy was somehow being blocked&nbsp;
from traveling to its most recent observer.&nbsp;

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:54.240
Having drawn a blank on trying to determine&nbsp;
SCP-096’s whereabouts, the Foundation eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.240 --> 00:11:00.420
turned to SCP-343 for his input. Naturally, the&nbsp;
powerful reality bender was reluctant as ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:06.600
to get involved. The Foundation insisted, knowing&nbsp;
that SCP-343’s omniscience meant he would already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:11.760
be aware of where they could find the missing&nbsp;
Shy Guy. He refused multiple times, admitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:15.960
he did indeed have the answer they were looking&nbsp;
for, but not wishing to divulge that information.&nbsp;

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:22.740
“Fine,” SCP-343 sighed, coming to a&nbsp;
compromise. “I can’t tell you exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:29.400
where 096 is. But when I tell you where&nbsp;
to look for answers, you’ll know: ASYNC.”&nbsp;

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:34.440
The researchers were stunned into silence.&nbsp;
Nobody in the Foundation had heard that name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:41.880
used in a long time. But SCP-343 was right – they&nbsp;
knew exactly what it meant. Back in the 1980s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:46.560
ASYNC was another shadowy organization that&nbsp;
had been investigating the existence of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:51.600
liminal space connected to reality. A&nbsp;
place they had called the Backrooms.&nbsp;

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:56.640
Gathering up a Mobile Task Force, the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation dispatched its agents to a site&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:01.200
that had long since been abandoned. They’d&nbsp;
kept a watchful eye over the disused lab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:07.140
keeping the public away, making sure nobody&nbsp;
stumbled in by accident and got trapped. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:12.900
the MTF commander gave the word, the outdated&nbsp;
80s technology was fired up, and ASYNC’s great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:18.420
achievement was reactivated. They had constructed&nbsp;
a portal into the Backrooms. Moving in formation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:25.620
the MTF operatives filed into the empty yellow&nbsp;
space, unsure if they’d find SCP-096 alive… or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:30.180
if it would even want to come back.
Meanwhile, in the Backrooms Level 0,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:36.240
only the Shy Guy remained - having completely&nbsp;
annihilated poor, unfortunate Adam. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:42.120
enjoying the solitude once again, knowing that&nbsp;
now, nobody was here to see him. Until one wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:51.060
step changed everything: He noclipped from Level&nbsp;
0 to Level 1, where he’d have a lot more company…&nbsp;

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:59.460
Now go and check out “SCP-096 VS SCP-343”&nbsp;
and “SCP-096 VS SCP-106” for more!

